<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24727" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-vĕnustus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Not elegant</i> or <i>graceful</i>,
				<i>ungraceful</i>, <i>not
			beautiful</i>, <i>unattractive</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scortillum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					10, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non invenustus actor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Brut. 67, 237</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">res,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					12, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arbustum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					5, 6, 37</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			(Without Venus, i. e.) <i>Unfortunate in love</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">invenustae sine munditia et sumptu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Poen. 1, 2, 37</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">homo invenustus aut infelix,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					And. 1, 5, 10</span></i>
			 Don. ad loc.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-vĕnustē</span></b> ,
				<i>not elegantly</i>, <i>ungracefully</i> (postAug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non invenuste dici videtur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 1, 6, 27</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ludere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 17, 12, 3</span></i>
			; App. de Mundo, p. 70.</div>
